3. Architecture
Student / Parent / Staff browser
              │
              ▼
     Next.js app and API routes
       │        │          │
       ▼        ▼          ▼
 Supabase    Supabase    AI provider
 Auth + DB   Storage     (server only)
       │
       └── Row Level Security policies
The browser should never receive service-role credentials or AI provider secrets. Enforce access rules in the database as well as in the UI. Route AI requests through the server, retrieve only resources the student is allowed to access, and include source titles or page references when available.
For the first version, resource search can be simple: staff-uploaded text excerpts or manually prepared notes linked to resources. Add automated PDF text extraction and semantic search only if the basic flow is working early enough.
4. Data model
Use UUID primary keys and timestamps. Keep student learning records separate from account profiles.
Table	Main fields
profiles	id (Auth user ID), full_name, role, preferred_language, created_at
student_profiles	user_id, grade, school_name (optional)
parent_student_links	parent_user_id, student_user_id, status, created_at
subjects	id, grade, name, description, sort_order, published
chapters	id, subject_id, title, sort_order, published
topics	id, chapter_id, title, sort_order, published
resources	id, topic_id (nullable), chapter_id, title, storage_path, mime_type, uploaded_by, published
topic_progress	student_user_id, topic_id, status, completed_at, updated_at
quizzes	id, topic_id, title, published, created_by
quiz_questions	id, quiz_id, prompt, options (JSON), correct_answer, explanation, sort_order
quiz_attempts	id, quiz_id, student_user_id, score, started_at, submitted_at
quiz_responses	attempt_id, question_id, answer, is_correct
tutor_sessions	id, student_user_id, tutor_user_id, starts_at, meeting_url, notes
scholarship_items	id, title, description, eligibility, deadline, url, published
tutor_conversations	id, student_user_id, created_at
tutor_messages	id, conversation_id, sender_role, content, source_refs, created_at


Do not store unnecessary personal details. For quiz questions, avoid exposing the correct answer to students before submission; enforce that in server queries rather than relying on hidden UI fields.
5. Roles and access
Use Supabase Auth for sign-in, and a profiles.role field for the initial roles: student, parent, tutor, and admin.
- Student: Read published learning content; edit only their own progress, quiz attempts, and conversations.
- Parent: Read progress only for students with an active parent_student_links record. Parents cannot edit student progress.
- Tutor: Read assigned students and manage tutoring-session details. For the MVP, keep student assignment explicit.
- Admin: Manage curriculum, resources, quizzes, users, and scholarship entries.
Implement database Row Level Security policies for every table. Treat the role shown in the browser as display information, not authorization. Admin role changes and parent–student links should be performed through a trusted server action or a restricted admin workflow.
For students under 18, make parent linking explicit and collect the minimum information needed. Before inviting real students, decide who handles consent, account recovery, data retention, and requests to delete or correct data.
